;; The registry for BOTH minted-oneof refusal fixtures.
;;
;; One file for two mints on purpose: a registry may legitimately carry pins for
;; messages a given mint file does not declare — `apply-numbering` looks up only
;; what it is asked for — so sharing it keeps the two cases differing in exactly
;; one input, which is what makes each refusal attributable to its own mint.
;;
;; Every field named by either fixture is pinned here. A refusal on either input
;; is therefore about the ONEOF and never about a missing pin, which is a
;; different refusal with a different message.
{"pgbad.Ping" {"seq" 6}
 "pgbad.Reading" {"raw" 5, "scaled" 9}}
